; specs/course/vibecoding.t27 -- the t27 course "Vibecoding from zero": describe it, run it, let a test judge it
; Source of truth for apps/website/scripts/course-from-spec.mjs (gHashTag/trinity), which reads
; it the way it reads specs/course/ai-numbers.t27: the constant schema, every test block below, every
; widget in specs/widgets/gallery.t27, every lesson spec compiled clean, the Russian bundle named
; by specs/course/vibecoding-ru.t27. It writes this course into src/lib/course.generated.ts (the
; page at #/vibecoding) and a byte-identical copy of this file at public/learn/vibecoding.t27.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN). The Russian words live in the bundle.

; WHAT THE COURSE IS: course 12 of specs/course/courses.t27, 27 lessons in 9 modules of 3. It
; starts from zero: a reader who has never programmed and has an editor with an AI agent beside
; it. The plan is specs/course_recipe/vibecoding-plan.t27. Modules 1 to 3 give the idea, the
; desk and the save points of git. Modules 4 to 6 are the craft: prompting, the working loop
; and a test as the judge. Modules 7 to 9 build: the parts of an agent, a first bot and an own
; project. Every lesson opens one widget and one spec.

; WHAT THE COURSE DOES NOT DO: it says no income range, no percent of graduates, no market size,
; no growth rate and no success story that a run does not back, and it copies no hand-written
; TypeScript or Python. Every number on a page is a constant of the lesson's spec, an arithmetic
; fact (3 x 3 x 3 = 27) or a count the player prints. The examples are made up and say so.

; WHY 27: 3 cubed lessons, the size of a TRI-27 word. Changing the shape changes the tests.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

